y for recovery and overall health. These supplements are particularly crucial for individuals with specific health conditions, such as diabetes, where maintaining proper nutrition is essential for managing their health effectively. The integration of nutritional support into the recovery process is a key component of successful outcomes following bariatric surgery [Data: Entities (8442, 2404); Relationships (3725, 2404)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Research contributions from medical journals\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Medical journals such as Lancet Diabetes & Endocrinology and Obesity Surgery have published significant research on the outcomes of bariatric surgery, including its effects on Type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular health. These studies provide valuable insights into the long-term benefits and risks associated with surgical interventions, helping to inform clinical practices and guidelines. The ongoing research in this field is crucial for advancing knowledge and improving treatment protocols for patients undergoing bariatric surgery [Data: Entities (5398, 6036); Relationships (14898, 11581)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Potential complications associated with bariatric surgery\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Bariatric surgery, while effective, is not without risks. Patients may experience complications such as nutritional deficiencies, gallstones, and hypoglycemia, particularly if post-operative dietary guidelines are not followed. Understanding these potential complications is essential for healthcare providers to monitor and manage patients effectively. The emphasis on nutritional control and regular follow-ups is critical to mitigate these risks and ensure successful recovery [Data: Entities (6033, 6034, 8760); Relationships (8762, 8761)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"The role of dietary recommendations in recovery\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Dietary recommendations are a fundamental aspect of the post-bariatric surgery recovery process. Patients typically transition through various dietary phases, starting from a liquid diet to solid foods, which is crucial for healing and adapting to the changes in their digestive system. Adhering to these dietary guidelines helps prevent complications and supports weight loss efforts. The structured approach to dietary reintroduction is essential for achieving optimal health outcomes post-surgery [Data: Entities (8431, 5963); Relationships (15352, 15353)].\"\n        }\n    ]\n}", "input": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n